    "questions": {
      "o1_f1": "In the supplied Rayleigh–Taylor instability snapshot, consider the complete supplied three-dimensional mesh. Investigate the vertical extent of the intermediate-density region. Use all cells, with arithmetic means of vertex values for point fields. Define c from cell density normalized by its sample minimum and maximum; use 4c(1-c) as a descriptive mixing-weight field. Measure width along the z axis as the weighted root-mean-square distance from its weighted center. Multiply the stated spatial weight by cell volume and normalize by its sum. Report the numerical width, and the weighted center coordinate.",
      "o2_f1": "In the supplied Rayleigh–Taylor instability snapshot, consider the complete supplied three-dimensional mesh. Investigate the vertical extent of the intermediate-density region. Use all cells, with arithmetic means of vertex values for point fields. Define c from cell density normalized by its sample minimum and maximum; use 4c(1-c) as a descriptive mixing-weight field. Multiply the stated spatial weight by cell volume and normalize by its sum. Choose and explain the remaining quantitative definition. Report the numerical width, and the weighted center coordinate.",
